    "updated_at": "2017-01-25T22:44:59Z",
    "body": "What parts of the spec are you referring to? Are you referring to the examples? If so, that's just how JavaScript works: you don't need to specify arguments you're not going to use (and usually it's bad practice to do so).\r\n\r\nIf you're interested in what arguments get passed to these callbacks, please read the places in the spec where they are invoked, instead of examples showing how to use them.",
