    "created_at": "2017-01-25T23:12:12Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-01-25T23:12:12Z",
    "body": "> They differ, the DOM is a different standard, if it must be read at least a link must be present in the HTML spec\r\n\r\nThere are links all over the custom elements section :).\r\n\r\n>  but the example has a different list of argument than the one specified in the DOM implementation.\r\n\r\nYes, as I stated above, in JavaScript, you don't need to specify arguments you're not going to use (and usually it's bad practice to do so). One of those examples uses 0/4 arguments, and the other uses 3/4, so that's how many the example specifies.",
